      "section_kind": "interpretive_questions",
      "section_title": "Interpretive Questions",
      "text": "Galatians cites Abraham's reckoned trust and blessing of nations, contrasts promise and Torah chronology, and focuses seed language on Messiah. Supports gentile inclusion without permitting appropriation that makes Jews strangers to Abraham or their scriptures. Romans coordinates Genesis 15 and 17 so Abraham's trust is reckoned before the later circumcision sign. Grounds gentile inclusion without recasting Jewish circumcision as worthless or shameful.",
